<title>SINGAPORE: Nortel gets US$70 mln Malaysia contract.</title>
<headline>Nortel gets US$70 mln Malaysia contract.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canada's Northern Telecom Ltd (Nortel) said on Friday it has been awarded a US$70 million contract by Malaysia's Binariang Sdn Bhd to supply DMS digital switching systems to the Maxis wireline telephone network.</p>
<p>In a staement, Nortel said the switches will equip Maxis with digital technology for the handling of local, toll and international voice and data traffic.</p>
<p>Nortel said this will be its first switching contract in Malaysia.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 870-3080)</p>
</text>
